    "turn_text": "This is the backlash over the quarantine. Now the capitalists closed, but that hasn't stopped all these people from gathering this morning. About a thousand are expected. It's been a lot of music, a lot of chanting. And a lot of signs, a lot of pro-Donald Trump signs, a lot of anti-governor rules signs. And a lot of signs saying they want Pennsylvania to get back to work. Now, today's rally is a mix of several groups that have decided to meet here today. Some organizers have asked people to stay in their cars, to wear masks, to keep six feet apart. Obviously, that is not happening. We did ask people who are not wearing masks. Why? They said they're not scared of the virus and if they get it, they'll beat it. Now what they want, they want Pennsylvania to get back to work. They want these restrictions lifted. Now just last week, Governor Wolf outlined a plan to get to state up and running, but there was no timetable with that.",
