    "turn_text": "Facebook has long been a favorite organizing tool for activists, but the social media network is saying it will delete events that violate state orders about staying at home, including events that organize protests. A Facebook spokesperson said per Politico, events that defy government's guidance on social distancing aren't allowed on Facebook. According to the New York Post, Facebook removed events in New Jersey, California, and Nebraska, organized by lockdown protesters. Next up, we'll have Rachel's interview with Representative Andy Viggs.",
