    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/3/83261.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 32,
    "turn_text": "Well, what we're doing is we're trying to put together ideas to the President about how to incentivize This is my role. This is what I view my role as being, how to incentivize the states to get going and opening these businesses and the economy in their states. And that's what I'm doing. And that's a lot of what we're talking about now with maybe a few more specifics thrown in. And we're debating that. I'm hopeful. I'm just hopeful that the American people, which are starting to see Rachel stand up and make claim on their rights, making claim for the economy, understanding that they don't want to spread a virus. But what they also don't want to do is lose life savings or lose their employment. And these are small business owners that want to get back to work. That's what I'm trying to emphasize in the President. I'm trying to to give anecdotal stories of folks that are losing their businesses to the administration.",
