  {
    "episode_id": 83261,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/3/83261.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 34,
    "turn_text": "Well, I mean, this morning early, a medical group told me, they sent me information, telling me that they had basically reduced salaries enormously in order to try to keep their employees on. They have also They basically have gone from maybe a month or two backlog in visits to same day visits because that's how few people come in anymore. I talked to them. I talked to builders, home builders, big industry in Arizona. They've got enough in their pipeline to last three months. But when you get four or five months out, there'll be no pipeline because nobody's buying houses now. When company told me they went from over 100 houses in March, but they're down to a negative seven in April. Why? Because people are canceling contracts because they no longer feel they can afford it. It has had a tremendous impact on the economy here. And it's quite frankly, we're seeing that all around the country as I talk to people from all over the country.",
